:"text"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"title":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/memberindices","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The indices of the set bits of one stored row, ascending, read in place: a column’s member"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices, or a vertex’s column indices ("},{"code":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). No copy and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocation, unlike a "},{"code":"BitSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It shares the matrix’s words copy-on-write, so a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutation of the matrix leaves it unchanged."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}]}}}